slug: spinal-and-general-measures
title: Spinal Mobility and General Measures — Schober, Chest Expansion, Occiput-Wall, Grip and BMI
area: Skills · Measurement
level: Foundation
best: 2nd year onwards
minutes: 12
hook: A tape measure can track spinal stiffness, lung expansion and sarcopenia better than the eye. Learn the five simple measures that every clinic should have. || Tape measure rindi spine ki sakhti, phephron ke phailao aur sarcopenia ko aankh se behtar track kar sakti hai. Woh paanch aasan measures seekhein jo har clinic mein hone chahiye.
goal: By the end, you'll perform the modified Schober, chest expansion and occiput-to-wall tests, grip strength and BMI/waist measurement and say what each result means. || End tak aap modified Schober, chest expansion aur occiput-to-wall tests, grip strength aur BMI/waist measurement karenge aur batayenge ke har result ka kya matlab hai.

say: Spine and chest stiffness are best tracked with **simple, repeatable measures**. The **modified Schober** marks the dimples of Venus (the PSIS) then 10 cm above and 5 cm below and measures how much the 15 cm grows when the patient bends forward (it should reach at least 20 cm). **Chest expansion** is measured at the 4th intercostal space (at the nipple line) after full breath out and in; at least 2.5 cm is normal. The **occiput-to-wall distance** is 0 cm in a normal spine. || Spine aur chest ki sakhti ko **aasan, repeatable measures** se behtar track karte hain. **Modified Schober** dimples of Venus (PSIS) ko mark kar ke 10 cm upar aur 5 cm neeche mark karta hai aur naapta hai ke aage jhukne par 15 cm kitna barhta hai (kam az kam 20 cm hona chahiye). **Chest expansion** 4th intercostal space (nipple line) par poori saans nikalne aur andar lene ke baad naapi jati hai; kam az kam 2.5 cm normal hai. **Occiput-to-wall distance** normal spine mein 0 cm hoti hai.
analogy: The modified Schober is like marking two dots on a balloon and watching how far apart they get when you blow it up. A stiff spine (ankylosing spondylitis, for example) is a balloon that will not stretch: the dots barely move apart. || Modified Schober ghubare par do nuqtay lagane aur phulane par un ka faasla dekhne jaisa hai. Sakht spine (maslan ankylosing spondylitis) aisa ghubara hai jo phailta nahi: nuqtay mushkil se door hotay hain.
demo: limb-measurements/modified-schober :: Modified Schober test :: Standing: mark the PSIS dimples, then 10 cm above and 5 cm below. Ask for maximum forward bend with straight knees and measure the marks again: the 15 cm should reach at least **20 cm** (an increase of 5 cm or more). Less suggests reduced lumbar flexion. || Khare hokar: PSIS dimples mark karein, phir 10 cm upar aur 5 cm neeche. Seedhe ghutnon ke saath zyada se zyada aage jhukne ko kahein aur marks dobara naapein: 15 cm kam az kam **20 cm** (5 cm ya zyada izafa) hona chahiye. Kam ho to lumbar flexion kam hai.
demo: limb-measurements/chest-expansion :: Chest expansion :: Hands on the head, tape around the chest at the 4th intercostal space (nipple line). Ask for a full breath out and then in, and read the difference. Use the **Chest** option to compare "Normal" with "Reduced" (for example ankylosing spondylitis or lung disease). || Haath sar par, tape chest ke gird 4th intercostal space (nipple line) par. Poori saans bahar aur phir andar lene ko kahein aur farq parhein. **Chest** option se “Normal” ko “Reduced” (maslan ankylosing spondylitis ya phephron ki bimari) se compare karein.
check: The modified Schober measurement goes from 15 cm to 17 cm on full forward bend. What does it suggest? || Modified Schober measurement poori aage jhukne par 15 cm se 17 cm ho jati hai. Yeh kya batata hai?
ok: Reduced lumbar flexion (normal is 5 cm or more of increase); look for causes such as inflammatory back pain || Lumbar flexion kam hai (normal 5 cm ya zyada izafa); inflammatory back pain jaisi wajahein dhoondein || Yes — a 2 cm increase is well below normal and, with other features, can fit axial spondyloarthritis. || Haan — 2 cm izafa normal se bohat kam hai aur doosri features ke saath axial spondyloarthritis se milta hai.
no: Normal flexion || Normal flexion || Normal is at least 20 cm. || Normal kam az kam 20 cm hai.
no: Hypermobility || Hypermobility || Hypermobility would give a larger increase. || Hypermobility mein zyada izafa hota.
demo: limb-measurements/occiput-wall :: Occiput-to-wall distance :: Heels and buttocks against the wall, eyes level. Measure the horizontal gap between the back of the head and the wall: normal is **0 cm**. A gap above about 2 cm suggests a thoracic kyphosis or a stiff spine such as in spondylitis. || Heels aur buttocks deewar se lagi, aankhein level. Sar ke peechay aur deewar ke beech horizontal gap naapein: normal **0 cm** hai. Takriban 2 cm se zyada gap thoracic kyphosis ya spondylitis jaisi sakht spine batata hai.
demo: limb-measurements/grip-strength :: Grip strength :: Seated, shoulder by the side, elbow at 90° and the forearm neutral; squeeze the dynamometer as hard as possible for about 3 seconds, three trials. Low grip strength is **under 27 kg in men and 16 kg in women** (EWGSOP2) and is a screen for sarcopenia and a predictor of frailty. || Baithe hue, shoulder side mein, elbow 90° aur forearm neutral; dynamometer ko jitna zor se ho takriban 3 seconds dabayein, teen trials. Low grip strength **mardon mein 27 kg aur aurton mein 16 kg se kam** (EWGSOP2) hai aur sarcopenia ki screening aur frailty ka predictor hai.
compare: Five measures, five questions || Paanch measures, paanch sawal
head: Measure || Measure ;; Normal value || Normal value ;; Think of… if abnormal || Agar abnormal ho to…
row: Modified Schober || Modified Schober ;; 15 cm → at least 20 cm || 15 cm → kam az kam 20 cm ;; Axial spondyloarthritis, lumbar stiffness, pain guarding || Axial spondyloarthritis, lumbar sakhti, dard ki guarding
row: Chest expansion || Chest expansion ;; At least 2.5 cm (often 4–5 cm) || Kam az kam 2.5 cm (aksar 4–5 cm) ;; Ankylosing spondylitis, lung disease, rib stiffness || Ankylosing spondylitis, phephron ki bimari, rib ki sakhti
row: Occiput-to-wall || Occiput-to-wall ;; 0 cm || 0 cm ;; Thoracic kyphosis, spondylitis, osteoporotic fracture || Thoracic kyphosis, spondylitis, osteoporotic fracture
row: Grip strength || Grip strength ;; Low if under 27 kg (men) or 16 kg (women) || Mardon mein 27 kg aur aurton mein 16 kg se kam low ;; Sarcopenia, frailty, malnutrition, neurological weakness || Sarcopenia, frailty, malnutrition, neurological kamzori
row: BMI and waist || BMI aur waist ;; BMI 18.5–24.9; waist risk above about 94 cm (men) or 80 cm (women) || BMI 18.5–24.9; waist risk takriban 94 cm (mard) ya 80 cm (aurtein) se upar ;; Cardiometabolic risk, under-nutrition, exercise planning || Cardiometabolic risk, under-nutrition, exercise planning
mistake: **Wrong landmarks and uncooperative breathing.** For the Schober, the dimples of Venus (PSIS) must be found by palpation, not by eye, and the marks must be re-measured *with the knees straight*, or flexion is overestimated. For chest expansion, instruct "maximum breath out, then maximum breath in", not "take a big breath", and measure at the same spot every time. For grip, always use the same dynamometer handle position and the same arm position. || **Ghalat landmarks aur be-dhyani se saans.** Schober ke liye dimples of Venus (PSIS) palpation se dhoondein, aankh se nahi, aur marks *seedhe ghutnon ke saath* dobara naapein, warna flexion zyada aankhi jati hai. Chest expansion ke liye “poori saans bahar, phir poori saans andar” kahein, “bari saans lein” nahi, aur har baar wohi jagah naapein. Grip ke liye hamesha dynamometer handle ki wohi position aur wohi arm position rakhein.
check: Why is the grip dynamometer position kept the same every time? || Grip dynamometer ki position har baar ek jaisi kyun rakhte hain?
ok: Grip force depends on handle width and arm position, so changes would alter the result || Grip force handle ki chorai aur arm position par depend karti hai, is liye tabdeeli result badal deti hai || Yes — standardisation is what makes a change between visits trustworthy. || Haan — standardisation hi visits ke beech tabdeeli ko bharosay ke qabil banati hai.
no: To make the patient squeeze harder || Patient ko zyada zor se dabane ke liye || Position does not motivate the patient. || Position patient ko hausla nahi deti.
no: To protect the dynamometer || Dynamometer ki hifazat ke liye || The device is not at risk. || Device khatray mein nahi.
clinic: **Use the numbers for decisions.** Reduced chest expansion plus a positive Schober, an occiput-wall gap and inflammatory back pain (worse at rest, better with movement, morning stiffness over 30 minutes, under 40 years) → refer to rheumatology. Low grip strength in an older adult → screen for sarcopenia (also gait speed and chair stand) and start resistance training and protein advice. BMI and waist circumference help set safe exercise intensity and risk. || **Numbers ko faislon ke liye use karein.** Kam chest expansion, positive Schober, occiput-wall gap aur inflammatory back pain (aaraam mein zyada, harkat se behtar, subah ki sakhti 30 minute se zyada, 40 saal se kam umar) → rheumatology ko refer. Buzurg mein low grip strength → sarcopenia screen (saath gait speed aur chair stand) aur resistance training aur protein ki salah shuru karein. BMI aur waist circumference mehfooz exercise intensity aur risk tay karne mein madad dete hain.
evidence: Grip strength is a strong marker of overall health: low grip is associated with disability, longer hospital stays and mortality, and it is one of the first things measured in a sarcopenia work-up (EWGSOP2 cut-offs: under 27 kg for men and under 16 kg for women). The modified Schober has good reliability; chest expansion and occiput-wall are useful for tracking change, but the cut-offs do not diagnose by themselves. || Grip strength poori sehat ka mazboot marker hai: kam grip disability, hospital mein zyada qiyam aur maut se jura hai, aur sarcopenia work-up mein sab se pehle naapi jane wali cheezon mein se ek hai (EWGSOP2 cut-offs: mardon ke liye 27 kg se kam aur aurton ke liye 16 kg se kam). Modified Schober ki reliability achi hai; chest expansion aur occiput-wall tabdeeli track karne ke liye kaam ki hain, lekin cut-offs khud tashkhees nahi karte.
reveal: Why do we measure the occiput-to-wall distance with the heels against the wall? || Occiput-to-wall distance heels ko deewar se laga kar kyun naapte hain? || Because a standard posture makes the number comparable between visits and between people: heels and buttocks on the wall remove pelvic and hip compensation so that the distance reflects thoracic and cervical posture only. || Kyunke standard posture number ko visits aur logon ke beech comparable banati hai: heels aur buttocks deewar par ho to pelvic aur hip compensation hat jati hai aur faasla sirf thoracic aur cervical posture dikhata hai.
check: A patient's chest expansion is 1.5 cm with morning stiffness over an hour and a young age. What is a sensible next step? || Patient ki chest expansion 1.5 cm hai, subah ki sakhti ek ghantay se zyada aur umar kam. Samajhdaar agla qadam?
ok: Suspect inflammatory back disease and refer for medical assessment while keeping the spine mobile || Inflammatory back disease ka shak karein aur spine ko mobile rakhte hue medical assessment ke liye refer karein || Yes — this pattern needs rheumatology review; exercise and posture work remain useful in the meantime. || Haan — is pattern ko rheumatology review chahiye; is dauran exercise aur posture kaam faide mand rehte hain.
no: Reassure that it is normal || Tasalli dein ke normal hai || Under 2.5 cm is below normal. || 2.5 cm se kam normal se kam hai.
no: Start high-velocity spinal manipulation || High-velocity spinal manipulation shuru karein || Do not manipulate a suspected inflammatory spine. || Shak-e-inflammatory spine ko manipulate na karein.
safety: **Refer urgently** for a sudden loss of height or new thoracic pain after minor trauma in an older adult (vertebral fracture), back pain with fever, weight loss or a history of cancer, or severe breathlessness with reduced chest movement. Do not use manipulation or end-range loading on a suspected fragile or inflamed spine. || **Foran refer karein** buzurg mein maamooli chot ke baad achanak qad ka kam hona ya naya thoracic dard (vertebral fracture), kamar ka dard bukhar, wazan ghatne ya cancer ki history ke saath, ya saans ki shadeed takleef aur kam chest movement. Shak-e-fragile ya inflamed spine par manipulation ya end-range loading use na karein.
summary: Modified Schober (15 → at least 20 cm), chest expansion (at least 2.5 cm) and occiput-wall (0 cm) track spinal and chest stiffness. || Modified Schober (15 → kam az kam 20 cm), chest expansion (kam az kam 2.5 cm) aur occiput-wall (0 cm) spine aur chest ki sakhti track karte hain.
summary: Grip under 27 kg (men) or 16 kg (women) screens for sarcopenia; BMI and waist circumference guide risk and exercise planning. || Grip mardon mein 27 kg aur aurton mein 16 kg se kam sarcopenia screen karti hai; BMI aur waist circumference risk aur exercise planning ki rehnumai karte hain.
summary: Standardise every measure (landmarks by palpation, same posture and device) and refer inflammatory or fragile-spine patterns instead of manipulating. || Har measure ko standardise karein (landmarks palpation se, wohi posture aur device) aur inflammatory ya fragile-spine patterns ko manipulate karne ke bajaye refer karein.
card: Normal modified Schober result? || Normal modified Schober result? || 15 cm growing to at least 20 cm (an increase of 5 cm or more). || 15 cm barh kar kam az kam 20 cm (5 cm ya zyada izafa).
card: Normal chest expansion and where is it measured? || Normal chest expansion aur kahan naapi jati hai? || At least 2.5 cm (often 4–5 cm) at the 4th intercostal space (nipple line). || Kam az kam 2.5 cm (aksar 4–5 cm), 4th intercostal space (nipple line) par.
card: Low grip strength cut-offs (EWGSOP2)? || Low grip strength cut-offs (EWGSOP2)? || Under 27 kg in men and under 16 kg in women. || Mardon mein 27 kg se kam aur aurton mein 16 kg se kam.
card: What is the normal occiput-to-wall distance? || Normal occiput-to-wall distance? || 0 cm (above about 2 cm suggests thoracic kyphosis or spondylitis). || 0 cm (takriban 2 cm se zyada thoracic kyphosis ya spondylitis batata hai).
deeper: Limb measurements skill in the Skills Lab || /skills/limb-measurements || Practise Schober, chest expansion, occiput-wall and grip in 3D. || Schober, chest expansion, occiput-wall aur grip 3D mein practise karein.
deeper: Red flags screening lesson || /learn/red-flags-screening || When back pain needs urgent medical review. || Kamar ka dard kab urgent medical review chahta hai.
source: Cruz-Jentoft AJ, et al. Sarcopenia: revised European consensus on definition and diagnosis (EWGSOP2). Age Ageing. 2019;48:16–31. || sarcopenia EWGSOP2 grip strength cut-off
source: Macrae IF, Wright V. Measurement of back movement. Ann Rheum Dis. 1969;28:584–589. || Schober test modified measurement back movement
